# Writer 12 (session 7c, A4): today's output, kept as a marker (REFCORE-NOT-YET in spirit; HANDOVER "Refused
# REFCORE-NOT-YET": a non-linear hole term). L §5.14 A hole in a term: "Only the parts the take could reach under some
# reading of the holes merge, into one hole part with the total known; a part ranked after enough certainly-ranked
# parts to cover the outflow stays known". r is an int hole. Under every reading of r, k_if's, k_cmp's and k_mm's
# orders rank ania's part first (k_if: 0 against 1 or 2; k_cmp: false against true; k_mm: min(r, 0) <= 0 < 1 <= max(r,
# 0) + 1), so by the spec the 30.00 out is taken from ania's part alone; refcore decides an order only through linear
# forms (partswalk pterms_lin, tcmp, lex3), so it is stricter: each take merges both parts into one hole part of
# 70.00, as printed below (a hole, never a wrong value). k_open's order `(if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1) * r` ranks
# either way by r's sign: its hole part is right. When a rule for these lands, the first three lines change and the
# fourth stays. (Triage scratch a4/t_if, t_cmp, t_minmax, t_open, as one text.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind sav_if: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order (if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1) * ((if r > 0 then 1 else 0) + 1)
kind sav_cmp: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania then (r > r) else true
kind sav_mm: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania then min(r, 0) else max(r, 0) + 1
kind sav_open: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order (if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1) * r
place k_if: sav_if lives 2026-01-01..
place k_cmp: sav_cmp lives 2026-01-01..
place k_mm: sav_mm lives 2026-01-01..
place k_open: sav_open lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input out_day: date
input out_amt: money PLN
input r: int
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
move sp_if: transfers
  on out_day
  leg cash from k_if to world amount out_amt
move sp_cmp: transfers
  on out_day
  leg cash from k_cmp to world amount out_amt
move sp_mm: transfers
  on out_day
  leg cash from k_mm to world amount out_amt
move sp_open: transfers
  on out_day
  leg cash from k_open to world amount out_amt
ask q_if: bal(k_if, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(k_if, 2026-03-31) of tomek
ask q_cmp: bal(k_cmp, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(k_cmp, 2026-03-31) of tomek
ask q_mm: bal(k_mm, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(k_mm, 2026-03-31) of tomek
ask q_open: bal(k_open, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(k_open, 2026-03-31) of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  opening[k_if] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_if] of ania = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_if] of tomek = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_cmp] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_cmp] of ania = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_cmp] of tomek = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_mm] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_mm] of ania = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_mm] of tomek = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_open] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_open] of ania = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_open] of tomek = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  out_day = 2026-03-01
  out_amt = 30.00 PLN
  r = ?"which?"
=== expect
q_cmp: (?"k_cmp: 70.00 PLN may be ania's: which?" (k_cmp), ?"k_cmp: 70.00 PLN may be tomek's: which?" (k_cmp))
...
q_if: (?"k_if: 70.00 PLN may be ania's: which?" (k_if), ?"k_if: 70.00 PLN may be tomek's: which?" (k_if))
...
q_mm: (?"k_mm: 70.00 PLN may be ania's: which?" (k_mm), ?"k_mm: 70.00 PLN may be tomek's: which?" (k_mm))
...
q_open: (?"k_open: 70.00 PLN may be ania's: which?" (k_open), ?"k_open: 70.00 PLN may be tomek's: which?" (k_open))
...
